@canac I asked CD earlier this morning and he said that option was offered to the stakeholders. They said they were okay with the other labels! I'm going to go ahead and merge!

> Morning Katelyn,
At the meeting yesterday we gave her that option.  She got with Amanda and they agreed on the change and were ok with the other labels.

@canac Should we add a check in case someone were to navigate to the "new" request url if they did not have permission to create an MHA yet? Something similar to `NoEditAccess.tsx` and `NoRequestAccess.tsx`?

Although, I'm not sure how beneficial it would be since it wouldn't actually create a requestID for MHA. I just know we have pages to prevent someone from trying to edit a request when they don't have permission or accessing the report when they don't have eligibility. What do you think?

Other than that, this looks great!

@kegrimes Sorry, I meant Mark, not Matt! The request I was testing with on the test account had the location set to NYC. That bumps up the caps a little bit. I think that's why I'm seeing 95K and you were seeing 85K. And Mark is single, so that's why I was seeing the Maximum Allowable Salary for a single person and you're seeing the couple amount.

